# Story 35: Shell Mode (40s)
# Hook: Shell mode is a real terminal -- full color, full ANSI, nothing held back.
# Duration: 40s
# Source: story-035-shell-mode.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 6

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Shell mode is a real terminal -- full color, full ANSI, nothing held back.

[00:03.0 --> 00:08.0]
Start rysh and you're already in shell mode. The greater-than marker is your cue.

[00:08.0 --> 00:16.0]
Every command runs in the pane's own PTY-backed shell, exactly like the terminal you already know.

[00:16.0 --> 00:26.0]
Color and ANSI escapes come through untouched -- git status, ls with color, anything that paints the screen.

[00:26.0 --> 00:34.0]
Pipes, redirects, environment variables -- it's a full shell, not a sandbox.

[00:34.0 --> 00:40.0]
Shell mode is home base. Everything else is one double-Escape away.

